.TH SPIValue 2type 2026-08-14 "Linux"

.SH NAME
SPIValue \- Value of variable in piControl driver

.SH LIBRARY
piControl device driver ioctl interface

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <piControl.h>"
.sp
.B typedef struct SPIValueStr {
.BR "    __u16  i16uAddress;" "  /* Address of the variable in process image */"
.BR "    __u8   i8uBit;" "       /* which bit position, or whole byte */"
.BR "    __u8   i8uValue;" "     /* Value that was read or should be written */"
.B } SPIValue;
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

.TP
.I i16uAddress
This field contains the address of the variable in the process image.
.TP
.I i8uBit
This field contains the position of the bit to access. Values
.BR 0 " to " 7
select a single bit, values of
.B 8
or more select the whole byte.
.TP
.I i8uValue
This field contains the value that is to be read after a call to
.BR KB_GET_VALUE (2),
or the value that should be written with a call to
.BR KB_SET_VALUE (2).
If a bit should be written with
.BR KB_SET_VALUE (2),
then the only allowed values for this field are
.BR 0 " or " 1 .

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR ioctl (2),
.BR KB_GET_VALUE (2),
.BR KB_SET_VALUE (2)
